##! experimental.virtual_source experimental.persistence experimental.join_types experimental.givens experimental.access_modifiers
import "../index.malloy"

// FORK ADDITION (F4). This was previously recorded as a deliberate CUT: this
// page has no custom React component -- Lloyd renders it with Malloy's built-in
// table renderer -- and adding provider marks was taken to mean replacing his
// page with a bespoke component, which §5's style ruling forbids. That premise
// was wrong. His renderer already draws tagged columns, so availability can be
// added as one more column IN his table: additive, no component, no redesign.
// One row per title, so joining it cannot fan the table out.
// ⛔ THE STREAMING COLUMN WAS REVERTED 2026-08-05. A fork addition nested a raw
// `string_agg(provider_name)` beside each title here. On the ONE page the style
// ruling protects most it: listed nine entries collapsing to five services,
// offered Hulu to a visitor who does not subscribe to it, rendered a bare ∅ on
// ~15 rows, and widened Lloyd's table to 1416 against his own 1280 — failing
// every bullet of CHARTER §7.3 (one mark, personalised, hidden when you cannot
// watch it). CHARTER §2A item 7 had already CUT the provider mark from this
// page because it has no custom component to draw one properly. The mark lives
// on the poster surfaces (genre_pairs, next_watch) where it can be drawn right.
// This query is now Lloyd's again, byte for byte.
# artifact { title="People that worked together" givens {NAME='Tom Hanks'}}
query: works_together is movies -> works_with + {
  where: name ~ $NAME
  nest: by_title is {
    group_by: title
    aggregate: total_ratings
  }
}
